CleanLine GPT-6 Optimized 1.0.0

The CleanLine algorithm was developed by Tim Mullen. CleanLine V2 includes
a rewrite by Kay A. Robbins, integration by Arnaud Delorme, and testing by
Makoto Miyakoshi. Performance optimization and integration for this build
were led by Makoto Miyakoshi with programming and benchmarking assistance
from OpenAI GPT-6 through ChatGPT Work.

The Original mode refers to CleanLine 2.00 with newversion=1. It does not
refer to the historical CleanLine V1 algorithm. Mathematical signal
processing, automatic harmonics, F-test decisions, iterative convergence,
and overlap blending are preserved in both modes.

The package-qualified CleanLine source in +clgpt6original and
+clgpt6optimized is adapted from the verified SCCN Cleanline2.00.zip
reference. The parent cleanline.m and pop_cleanline.m expressly permit
GPL version 3 or later and invoke the V2 core. The archive's GPL v2 text
is retained in ORIGINAL_CLEANLINE_LICENSE.txt and discussed in
docs/LICENSING_AUDIT.md.

The four +clgpt6compat helpers are newly written compatibility
implementations of the required interfaces and equations. No original
Chronux or BCILAB source or binary is bundled. The ZIP contains no
participant EEG data.
